{
  // The in-game trader task-list group for each task: the client's per-task
  // `tierAccessory`. 0 renders as "Essential Tasks" (locale key
  // UI/Quests/TraderAccessoryGroup/Chain); 1-4 render as "Loyalty Level 1-4"
  // (UI/Quests/TraderAccessoryGroup/Tier1-Tier4). Operational (daily) tasks are
  // a separate client group and are not listed here.
  //
  // Display grouping only. A group is never an availability gate: tier 1-4
  // unlocks come from trader loyalty plus the progressionCounters pools, and
  // Essential tasks carry their own ordinary start conditions.
  //
  // Evidence: 1.1 PvE, PvP and Seasonal quest-list captures. Every task seen
  // in more than one mode had the same value in each (405 cross-mode pairs, no
  // disagreement), so each mode block lists every task tarkov.dev serves in that
  // mode with a captured value. Seasonal coverage therefore leans on the PvE
  // and PvP captures. Tasks absent from every capture are omitted, not guessed;
  // consumers must treat a missing entry as "group unknown". In-game check:
  // a 1.2.5 PvP Seasonal client lists Wet Job - Part 1 under "Essential Tasks"
  // and New Paths, Seizing the Initiative, Chemical Experiments and Metal Birds
  // under Peacekeeper "Loyalty Level 1".
  // Pool cross-check: each published progressionCounters pool's captured tasks
  // carry exactly that pool's loyaltyLevel here (tests/trader-task-groups.test.ts).
  // Proof: https://github.com/tarkovtracker-org/tarkov-data-overlay/blob/main/docs/GLOBAL_VARIABLE_MECHANICS.md
